.TH BIGINTMULFFT 3 "2026-09-24" "BigNums" "Library Functions Manual"
.nr HY 0
.ds AD l
.SH NAME
bigIntMulFFT \- multiply two big integers using verified FFT convolution
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include \(dqbignums.h\(dq
.sp
.BI "int bigIntMulFFT(BigInt *" "result" ", const BigInt *" "a" ","
.BI "    const BigInt *" "b" ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Multiplies a by b and stores the product in result.
The destination may be the same object as either or both inputs.
The inputs must be initialized; a distinct destination need not be.
.PP
Each limb is split into four base-256 digits.  A power-of-two complex FFT
convolution computes the product coefficients, using at most 8192 points.
Every rounded coefficient is checked against an exact modular convolution
modulo 998244353.  At 1024 limbs, every coefficient is at most 266342400,
less than the modulus, so this verification is deterministic.
If floating-point reconstruction fails, the exact modular coefficients are
used instead.  Carry propagation and capacity checks precede output assignment.
Zero products skip transforms.  Temporary heap buffers are freed before return.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 0 on success, INT_MAX if the product exceeds MAX_LIMBS, or \-1 on
allocation or transform failure.
Errors leave result unchanged.
No caller-side deallocation is required.
.SH NOTES
The running time is O(n log n), with n = a.size + b.size, including verification
and recovery.  Temporary heap storage is at most 320 KiB at 1024 limbs.
Verification adds three modular transforms to the three complex transforms.
The standalone complex FFT API remains available through complexFFT.h and
uses double precision without exact verification.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bigIntMulUInt_32 (3),
.BR fft (3),
.BR bignums (3),
.BR bignums (7)
